                "word": "philopena",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "77d73f1f-168d-4126-b5f9-16d91feb1103",
                        "entry_id": "353e8928-cff1-3f54-9469-0b0aa62d0071",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "philopenas"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "68ca5cbb-cfdc-3054-a12a-4ba5bf3fe5b5",
                        "entry_id": "353e8928-cff1-3f54-9469-0b0aa62d0071",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A game in which a person, on finding a double-kernelled almond or nut, may offer the second kernel to another person and demand a playful forfeit from that person to be paid on their next meeting. The forfeit may simply be to exchange the greeting \\\"Good-day, Philopena\\\" or it may be more elaborate. Philopenas were often played as a form of flirtation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e695e150-b98b-34a7-a256-ddfe3b2af2e5",
                        "entry_id": "353e8928-cff1-3f54-9469-0b0aa62d0071",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The occasion on which a philopena is forfeited; the forfeit paid."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2c7bde84-448d-32fb-8ea2-43363374c098",
                        "entry_id": "353e8928-cff1-3f54-9469-0b0aa62d0071",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A nut or almond with a double kernel, as used to set a philopena."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6eb854a7-359a-488b-8d18-8e51721e2d4e",
                        "source_entry_id": "353e8928-cff1-3f54-9469-0b0aa62d0071",
                        "source_sense_description": "A game",
                        "target_lang_word": "philippine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "philippine",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b4b8750-6320-3cd6-b6b3-1ef0676e119d",
                                        "entry_id": "519bb48d-2aa7-31de-85ea-892c65e78a21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Jeu qui consiste, quand on trouve une amande double, à la partager avec quelqu’un, et par la suite, pour gagner, à être le premier qui aborde l’autre en disant « Bonjour philippine »."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "106c7588-535c-326c-afce-cce2675f2030",
                                        "entry_id": "519bb48d-2aa7-31de-85ea-892c65e78a21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Une amande double."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dc618c3-6469-4fd9-9850-9c11caafcf53",
                                                "sense_id": "106c7588-535c-326c-afce-cce2675f2030",
                                                "text": "L’amande bessonne, jumelle ou philippine est un prétexte à toutes sortes de jeux joyeux…"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aeb54fbd-7569-3af2-bb7f-6560115af102",
                                        "entry_id": "519bb48d-2aa7-31de-85ea-892c65e78a21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mot qu’on dit quand deux personnes commencent à prendre la parole en même temps pour dire la même chose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db26bed2-6290-4b8a-ab91-3c9409ff40e9",
                                                "sense_id": "aeb54fbd-7569-3af2-bb7f-6560115af102",
                                                "text": "j'aurais du mal à te donner l'origine du truc, mais c'est un truc de gosses, quand on dit la même chose au même moment, on dit philippine et on fait un vœu."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
